    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n19310" root="سدر" body-key="s">
    
      Q. Q. 4 
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">اِسْمَدَرَّ بَصَرُهُ</span></b>  <i>His sight became weak,
in the manner described below, voce</i> <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">سَمَادِيرُ</span>. (S
in art. <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">سدر</span>, and M and K in art. <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">سمدر</span>.) It is of
the measure <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">اِفْمَعَلَّ</span>, from <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">السَّدَرُ</span>; (IKtt;) the <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">م</span>
being augmentative. (S.) See also <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">سَدِرَ</span>. ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b2- 
<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">اسمدرّت عَيْنُهُ</span> <i>His eye shed tears;</i> accord. to Lh;
but this is not known in the classical language.
(M in art. <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">سمدر</span>.)

